WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:09.600
How much of civilization is shaped by our&nbsp;
biology? How might our cities, transportation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:15.680
and technology look different if we weren’t a&nbsp;
group of nearly hairless primates? The video game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:23.040
Spore has the answers. Okay, well, maybe not the&nbsp;
answers — but Spore does offer an interesting case&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:29.440
study into the fundamentals of how a speculative&nbsp;
lifeform might build a society. In our first Spore&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:36.240
episode, we followed a lifeform from a microscopic&nbsp;
organism to the intelligent Curiousus Sapiens.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:42.560
In this episode, we’ll witness the ascent of&nbsp;
their civilization, and explore how the unique&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:48.880
biology of an alien like Curiousus Sapiens would&nbsp;
affect things like the design of clothing, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:55.280
schematics of vehicles, and shapes of buildings&nbsp;
in unexpected ways. We’ll begin with Tribal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:02.880
Stage and go all the way to Space, completing the&nbsp;
multi-billion-year-tale of Curiousus Sapiens. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:08.000
let’s return to Planet Curious, and&nbsp;
discover the finale of the story of life…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:17.440
After the early evolutionary stages, the birth&nbsp;
of society is underway — with Curiousus Sapiens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:23.120
building fires and early lodgings.&nbsp;
But is this the dawn of a wise people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:30.160
or a culture of warmongering tyrants? What path&nbsp;
will Curiosus Sapiens take in shaping the destiny&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:36.560
of their planet? Like the game’s biology, cultural&nbsp;
evolution in Spore is fairly simplified and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:42.960
exaggerated. ‘Tribal Stage’ seems to be a mesh&nbsp;
of various eras, but seems most comparable to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:49.360
hunter-gatherer culture. At this point in history,&nbsp;
Curious Sapiens appear only to have access to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:54.960
simple technologies quite similar to that of&nbsp;
early humans. It might seem surprising that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.960 --> 00:02:00.640
Curiosus Sapiens would converge on concepts like&nbsp;
pottery — but there is some precedent for this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:07.120
idea. On earth, certain technologies are ‘cultural&nbsp;
universals’ — meaning that numerous cultures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:12.560
invented a version of them independently from&nbsp;
one another. The sheer number of times disparate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.760
populations have invented something like pottery&nbsp;
indicates that when intelligent minds are faced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:23.440
with the same problem — similar answers might&nbsp;
emerge. Whether or not this would hold true for an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:29.840
alien in an alien environment is difficult to&nbsp;
say — but depending on the circumstances, Curious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:36.960
Sapiens inventing pottery is certainly possible.&nbsp;
As technology improves, Spore gives us the option&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:42.880
to determine the clothing of Curiousus Sapiens.&nbsp;
The question of what kind of clothes an emerging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:49.120
sapient alien species would wear — assuming they’d&nbsp;
wear clothing at all — is actually a tricky one.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:54.560
Clothing is so ubiquitous today for us Homo&nbsp;
Sapiens that we almost don’t think about it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.280
The initial invention of clothing was likely&nbsp;
tied to the climate, and served as a way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:05.040
protect our hairless bodies from the elements.&nbsp;
Yet compared to Earth, Planet Curious — like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:11.360
most planets in Spore — seems to have an extremely&nbsp;
temperate macroclimate, so it’s unlikely clothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:17.360
would develop for temperature control alone. Yet&nbsp;
clothing can also protect the body from specific&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:23.600
environmental hazards like pests, abrasive&nbsp;
substances, and other irritants. So, it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:29.760
possible that protective attire would first emerge&nbsp;
in Curiousus Sapiens in particularly vulnerable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:36.080
areas — like the base of their eye-stalks. Human&nbsp;
clothing also has various social functions across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:41.920
cultures, and some articles of alien clothing&nbsp;
could serve in these ways. Unlike humans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:47.520
Curiousus Sapiens have an elaborate display&nbsp;
structure sprouting from their shoulders, similar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:53.040
to the extravagant plumages of certain birds.&nbsp;
It’s not too big a leap to assume garments would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:58.800
be built around complementing these structures&nbsp;
— making them appear fuller and more impressive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:04.560
An emergent hunter-gatherer species would also&nbsp;
likely find value in various satchels or pouches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:10.560
to carry resources. And finally, aliens might&nbsp;
develop some articles of clothing with no apparent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:16.400
function whatsoever — either as reflections of&nbsp;
cultural trends or expressions of personal style.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:21.600
In the case of Curiousus Sapiens, clothing&nbsp;
choices would be limited by available&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:27.440
materials — which in this age would likely&nbsp;
comprise hides, grass, leaves, and shells.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:32.720
The end result is attire that certainly looks&nbsp;
pretty strange to our eyes… but a Curiousus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:40.000
Sapiens would likely find the eccentricities of&nbsp;
our clothing just as puzzling… As time passes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.920
Curiousus Sapiens fall into a rhythm within the&nbsp;
hunter-gatherer lifestyle, with obtaining food the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:51.920
most important task during this era. Historically,&nbsp;
permanent settlements on Earth rarely emerge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:57.680
until after the invention of agriculture and&nbsp;
domesticated plants. Spore skips over any mention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:03.680
of agriculture, but realistically we can assume&nbsp;
that Curiousus Sapiens have some early version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:09.680
of subsistence farming figured out. And Curiousus&nbsp;
Sapiens aren’t the only lifeforms to have achieved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:15.840
advanced intelligence. Across Planet Curious,&nbsp;
other species are building their own societies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.640
Different unrelated species all reaching the&nbsp;
same level of technological advancement during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:27.440
the exact same period isn’t particularly likely…&nbsp;
but this is how Spore functions. The question is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:32.240
how will Curiousus Sapiens choose to interact&nbsp;
with their new neighbors going forwards?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:38.480
To guide Curiousus Sapiens through this&nbsp;
new era, two tools are now available for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:44.400
construction — the spear and the wooden horn,&nbsp;
which looks like a kind of rudimentary flute.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:50.160
As far as early tools go, these are actually&nbsp;
fairly plausible. Spears are the oldest weapon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:56.880
we have an unambiguous archeological record of,&nbsp;
dating back to the Paleolithic age. Likewise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:02.960
mammoth bone flutes from the Paleolithic are the&nbsp;
oldest known musical instruments. Realistically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:08.720
however, the tools of a species like Curiousus&nbsp;
Sapiens would likely be different from our own.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:15.760
For one, since Curiousus Sapiens only have four&nbsp;
fingers instead of five, their musical instruments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:21.360
would likely look different, as they’d likely&nbsp;
only have access to a pentatonic scale instead of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:26.960
a heptatonic one when playing a wind instrument&nbsp;
— with five notes per octave instead of seven.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:32.720
Likewise, it’s interesting to deliberate on&nbsp;
whether a lifeform like Curiousus Sapiens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:38.080
would develop a spear in the first place. Humans&nbsp;
lack the claws and fangs of most top predators&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:43.840
in the animal kingdom, pressuring early humans to&nbsp;
invent tools to compete with the natural weaponry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:49.840
of other animals. Yet an unarmed Curiousus&nbsp;
Sapiens is already a formidable customer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:56.080
and might not need to be as creative. Still, it’s&nbsp;
possible that any emergent tool user would be able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:01.200
to puzzle out the basic concept that sticking&nbsp;
something sharp on the end of something long is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:06.560
a good way to deal damage while keeping yourself&nbsp;
out of harm’s reach. In either case, with their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:12.240
new tools, Curiousus Sapiens can now enchant&nbsp;
other species with their musical instruments…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:18.160
or impale them on the end of their spear. As&nbsp;
thinking social omnivores, Curiousus Sapiens make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:24.880
allies when they can. But when another species&nbsp;
attacks first, Curiousus Sapiens respond in kind.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:30.800
In a trend that sadly echoes our own history,&nbsp;
this early era is marked by frequent conflict...&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:37.360
But society is also changing in other ways.&nbsp;
Curiousus Sapiens are on the path towards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:44.320
creating a larger and more stable civilization —&nbsp;
a path laden with new developments. At this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:50.000
Curiousus Sapiens gain the ability to domesticate&nbsp;
animals — a crucial trait for emergent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:55.920
civilizations. There’s a lot that could be said&nbsp;
about animal domestication, but to simplify:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.920 --> 00:08:02.240
we humans began our animal domestication journey&nbsp;
with wolves before the agricultural revolution,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:07.360
then moved on to small herbivores like sheep&nbsp;
and goats once we began staying in one place for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:13.840
longer. Beasts of burden that could plow fields or&nbsp;
give you a ride like cows and horses came later.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:19.200
Curiousus Sapiens will begin their journey&nbsp;
with this small bird-like quadruped, harvesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:24.800
their feathers for clothing and construction&nbsp;
materials and their eggs for dietary consumption.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:31.120
Generations later, the second animal Curiousus&nbsp;
Sapiens domesticate is this large… horrifying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:36.720
spider-beast. These hardy giants might look&nbsp;
intimidating, but they’re actually quite docile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:41.040
and will fill the role of plow animals.&nbsp;
It’s worth noting that while, once again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:46.080
Spore never touches on agriculture, in order&nbsp;
for this sort of domestication to be possible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:51.040
Curiousus Sapiens must have begun the practice.&nbsp;
And with these animals in their corner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:56.480
the population can grow to new sizes, and&nbsp;
society itself can become more complex.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:03.440
New buildings are now available, like this&nbsp;
outlet for fishing spears — seemingly implying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:08.240
the emergence of small industries and the&nbsp;
increased specialization of tasks within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:15.200
Curious Sapiens society. And just looking at their&nbsp;
society, culture seems richer and more diverse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:20.320
with different Curious Sapiens sharing&nbsp;
ideas and playing musical instruments.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:25.920
After making one final alliance, Spore gives&nbsp;
us the option to advance to the next stage…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:34.960
Hurtling forwards in time, ‘Civilization Stage’&nbsp;
begins with the option to build a modern building.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:40.800
Once again, Spore’s timeline of historical change&nbsp;
is certainly a simplified one, as there are,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:46.880
historically, numerous steps between small&nbsp;
subsistence societies and an emergent industrial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:52.960
civilization. Likewise, Spore puts no limits&nbsp;
on this first building, letting you construct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:58.320
something truly absurd if you feel like it. Fun&nbsp;
as that can be, it’s interesting to consider what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:05.040
an early industrial house might look like for a&nbsp;
Curiousus Sapiens. Unlike humans Curiousus Sapiens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:10.480
are nest builders — and have been for the past&nbsp;
several hundred million years of their evolution.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:14.720
As a result, it’s possible that their instinct&nbsp;
for houses would be different from our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:20.080
own — building smaller, more low-to-the-grown&nbsp;
dwellings that evoke their ancestral nests.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:26.160
With a town hall constructed, the Curiousus&nbsp;
Sapiens debate the nature of their society.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:32.400
With a stable food supply, natural resources&nbsp;
like Spice — which flows from most planets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:39.040
in Spore — becomes the new valued commodity. The&nbsp;
value of Spice in Spore reminds me of the sci-fi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:45.120
world of Dune, and if my memory of that series&nbsp;
is accurate, a reliance on Spice might cause…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:51.920
problems. But for now, Curiousus Sapiens are a&nbsp;
young populace with their heads lost in the dream&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:57.920
of the future... On that note, Spore gives us the&nbsp;
option to design our first vehicle that will help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:04.080
with transporting the spice. As always, Spore&nbsp;
lets you design whatever absurd thing you want,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:10.320
but alien cars genuinely might not look like&nbsp;
we’d expect. Certain things like wheels could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:16.640
universal considering the constraints of physics.&nbsp;
Yet our vehicles reflect us more than we realize.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:22.560
Several studies have shown that when we look at&nbsp;
most cars, our brains’ facial recognition cortex&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:29.280
is activated. This isn’t a coincidence — cars are&nbsp;
designed to subtly resemble human faces to appeal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:35.440
to our pattern-seeking minds. And if Curiousus&nbsp;
Sapiens have similar instincts, it's likely their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:42.240
vehicles would subtly reflect the geometry of&nbsp;
their faces… With our first vehicle constructed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:48.480
the Spice can be gathered and transported — for&nbsp;
better or worse. In this era, other civilizations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:55.120
of Curiousus Sapiens have also emerged. We’ve&nbsp;
already seen this species, much like humans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.120 --> 00:12:00.800
has the potential for war and cooperation — so&nbsp;
the ultimate future of Planet Curious will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:06.480
determined by how well they can work together.&nbsp;
Contacting our closest neighbors, we can offer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:12.480
gifts, compliment them, or say their people&nbsp;
are ‘descended from limbless space slugs.’ Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:18.000
I’m no political expert, but I suspect one of the&nbsp;
first two options is a better tactic... Thanks to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:24.160
such savvy political acumen, the two civilizations&nbsp;
establish a trade route and begin the long road&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:31.280
towards a united future… As time passes, cities&nbsp;
become larger and full of new technologies. Thanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:37.440
to the steady force of negotiation, alliances form&nbsp;
— first with immediate neighbors, and then with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:44.480
more distant countries. As technology improves,&nbsp;
clothing evolves as well, featuring new textiles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:50.080
and construction materials. I tried to make the&nbsp;
post-industrial clothes of Curiousus Sapiens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:56.960
still vaguely echo earlier culture trends. Got&nbsp;
to keep those silly hats, after all. In time, we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:03.360
unlock the secrets of motorized flying machines,&nbsp;
and can design our first air vehicles. Here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:08.320
the constraints of things like wind resistance&nbsp;
might shape our craft into something similar to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:13.680
the planes we have on Earth, although just like&nbsp;
with their land vehicles, Curiousus Sapiens may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:18.960
build something that subtly reflects the geometry&nbsp;
of their faces. And with their natural stalk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:25.440
eyes and more flexible necks Curiousus Sapiens&nbsp;
likely have a greater visual field than humans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:29.600
so the cockpits of their aircrafts might&nbsp;
have more windows to the sides and back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:35.760
With aircrafts now soaring through the atmosphere,&nbsp;
the planet is more connected through trade than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:42.000
ever before. Achieving planetary peace through&nbsp;
careful management and negation is admittedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:46.560
not the most exciting way to play, but it’s&nbsp;
certainly worth it. At the end of this era,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:53.200
Curiousus Sapiens are united under one banner, and&nbsp;
looking towards the stars as their next horizon...&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.200 --> 00:14:02.960
And so, the final chapter, ‘Space Stage’, begins.&nbsp;
Curiousus Sapiens are no longer beholden to just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:08.320
a single, meager world. After designing a&nbsp;
spacecraft that follows the same aesthetic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:14.400
standards of the other vehicles, for the first&nbsp;
time, Curiousus Sapiens are free to explore beyond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:20.240
the protective atmosphere of their home. Traveling&nbsp;
to another planet in the system, the Sapiens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:25.840
discover a crashed vessel, and are lucky enough&nbsp;
to scan and replicate its interstellar drive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:32.080
From the perspective of the player, you&nbsp;
can zoom out and behold the entire galaxy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:38.400
spinning just like how it is in the title screen —&nbsp;
except now you can go to any part of it you like.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:44.560
That first moment when you realize the whole&nbsp;
galaxy is now yours to explore is pretty magical,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:51.760
and makes the scope of Spore feel so impossibly&nbsp;
vast. The galaxy is waiting, and the rest is up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:57.120
to you. Every one of these stars contains&nbsp;
their own system of orbiting planets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:02.080
which you can fly down to and visit. At the&nbsp;
time when Spore first came out, this kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:08.240
of procedurally generated universe was something&nbsp;
never really attempted before. At the same time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:14.880
such scale has its drawbacks. It’s hard not to&nbsp;
feel like, in a galaxy this large, nothing you do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:20.640
has much meaning. I know a lot of people’s least&nbsp;
favorite stage is Space Stage, and I understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:26.240
why. It’s easy to become disconnected from the&nbsp;
creature you started with billions of years ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:32.400
although perhaps that’s an unavoidable symptom of&nbsp;
a species becoming a galaxy-spanning civilization.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:39.840
Expanding across the cosmos, Curiousus Sapiens&nbsp;
gain the ability to build self-assembling colonies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:46.080
on barren worlds. In their expansion, they search&nbsp;
for radio wave frequencies that might signal the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:51.760
presence of technologically-advanced life like&nbsp;
themselves. On our planet, we’re scanning the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:57.440
stars for alien life by searching for similar&nbsp;
frequencies — although with our limited range,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.440 --> 00:16:03.360
so far, we’ve found nothing but silence. Yet&nbsp;
Curiousus Sapiens can journey much further out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:09.520
across the stars, and eventually they encounter&nbsp;
other intelligent, space-faring life who rose from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:16.400
the primordial soup just like they did. In time,&nbsp;
Curiousus Sapiens even unlock the secrets of life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:22.080
and can create creatures to populate newly&nbsp;
terraformed worlds. This kind of power can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:28.000
be used to create bizarre forms of life,&nbsp;
as biology becomes an infinite playground.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:33.680
In the words of science fiction author Arthur&nbsp;
C. Clarke, “any sufficiently advanced technology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:39.360
is indistinguishable from magic,” and that&nbsp;
adage holds true here. It can also be used&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:44.720
more responsibly, and we’d have to hope such&nbsp;
an advanced form of life would be sensible with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:51.760
their power. Looking forwards, Curious Sapiens&nbsp;
will ascend to a civilization we can’t fathom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:55.680
transcending technology beyond&nbsp;
the scope of our limited minds…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:57.360 --> 00:17:03.200
By design, Spore skips over many of the stages&nbsp;
of history, condensing and exaggerating the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:08.960
long road of technological advancement. Yet&nbsp;
the game does explore a surprising number of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:15.360
the universal principles of how civilizations and&nbsp;
technology change over time. I know not everybody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:21.200
likes the later stages of Spore compared to Cell&nbsp;
and Creature, and I can understand that. Still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:26.560
the novelty of guiding a speculative creature&nbsp;
through their technological advancement is pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:32.960
intriguing even all these years later. Like I said&nbsp;
in part one, I’d love to see another high-profile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:38.640
game tackle something similar, as I feel there’s&nbsp;
real potential for a modern take on this concept.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:44.160
As always, thanks for watching.&nbsp;
If you enjoyed this entry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:49.360
please lend your support to help make these&nbsp;
videos possible by liking, subscribing, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:59.840
hitting the notification icon to stay up to date&nbsp;
on all things Curious. See you in the next video.

